<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $226.7 mln April 10.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $226.7 mln April 10.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $226.7 million deficit on April 10 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON APRIL 10</p>
<p>Exports: $172.7 million</p>
<p>Imports: $252.7 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $214.5 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $361.2 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $226.7 million</p>
<p>ARPIL DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.448 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.674 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.021 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.777 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $18 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
